= Solution
{parent=1}

Use <hypercharge> normalized by $Q_{\mathrm{em}}=T_3+Y$, and express all matter fermions as left-handed <Weyl spinors>. Thus $u^c,d^c,e^c$ denote the charge conjugates of the right-handed <Standard Model fermions>; the superscript $c$ is unrelated to the antiparticle marker $(A)$. Each <chiral superfield> contains a <complex scalar field> and a <Weyl spinor>, while each <vector superfield> contains a <gauge boson> and a <gaugino>. The complete propagating content of the <Minimal supersymmetric Standard Model> before <electroweak symmetry breaking> is:

